WEBVTT

00:02.600 --> 00:05.800
"It seems today that all you see

00:05.900 --> 00:09.200
"is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:09.300 --> 00:12.900
"But where are those good,
old-fashioned values

00:13.100 --> 00:15.500
"on which we used to rely?

00:16.000 --> 00:18.800
"Lucky there's a family guy

00:19.300 --> 00:22.500
"Lucky there's a man who'll
positively tell you

00:22.600 --> 00:24.200
"all the things that make us

00:24.300 --> 00:25.600
"laugh 'n' cry

00:25.900 --> 00:30.700
"He's a family guy"

00:37.900 --> 00:39.700
- I'm Morley Safer.
- I'm Mike Wallace.

00:39.800 --> 00:41.800
- I'm Ed Bradley.
- I'm Lesley Stahl.

00:41.900 --> 00:43.900
And one of you is hung like an elf.

00:46.200 --> 00:49.500
I feel so naughty.
Lois, what are you doing?

00:49.600 --> 00:50.900
Neither of us is drunk.

00:54.300 --> 00:55.400
Knock it off!

00:56.900 --> 01:00.600
Oh, my God! I found a lump!
A breast lump!

01:03.100 --> 01:06.500
The important thing is to stay calm.
It's probably nothing, honey.

01:06.600 --> 01:09.500
That's easy for you to say.
You get to keep both your cans.

01:09.600 --> 01:12.700
Peter, don't talk like that!
You'll see a doctor tomorrow and...

01:12.800 --> 01:15.200
No. I'm not gonna see a doctor, Lois.

01:15.400 --> 01:19.200
The healthiest thing we can do is just
ignore this and pretend it doesn't exist.

01:19.300 --> 01:21.100
Just like we do with the squid.

01:24.400 --> 01:26.300
Earthquake.
Truck going by.

01:27.300 --> 01:30.100
I'm gonna be fine.
Nothing to worry about.

01:33.900 --> 01:35.100
Morning.

01:37.200 --> 01:39.500
Give it to me straight, Doc.
How long do I have?

01:39.600 --> 01:42.100
Mr. Griffin, I'd say you have
about a month to live.

01:42.700 --> 01:46.600
But what the hell do I know?
I've been sued by every patient I ever had.

01:46.700 --> 01:48.400
Look at the size of this file.

01:48.500 --> 01:50.800
This is... Wow.

01:53.100 --> 01:55.100
Let's just wait for the test results.

01:56.600 --> 01:59.300
Finish up, honey.
Then I'll put you down for a nice nap.

01:59.400 --> 02:02.300
No! I shall put you down
for a nap, Mother!

02:03.600 --> 02:04.600
Blast!

02:05.600 --> 02:07.400
I'm so worried about your father.

02:07.500 --> 02:09.700
You mean because
he's a borderline alcoholic?

02:09.800 --> 02:12.000
No. Mommy's made peace with that.

02:12.100 --> 02:14.400
Because he's got a lump on his booby.

02:14.500 --> 02:17.100
Chris, that's a terrible word, "booby."

02:17.400 --> 02:21.300
Mom, Debbie Miller's dad had a lump
on his breast, and he turned out okay.

02:21.400 --> 02:23.700
Really? Who's Debbie Miller?

02:23.900 --> 02:25.300
A girl I just made up.

02:26.200 --> 02:28.900
Look. Here they are. My family.

02:29.300 --> 02:33.000
Guys, I don't say this often enough,
but I'm gonna die.

02:33.100 --> 02:35.600
Oh, my God.
High five! Anyone?

02:35.900 --> 02:36.900
Anyone?

02:37.000 --> 02:40.700
You can't die! Who's gonna take me
to the Father-Son dance?

02:40.800 --> 02:42.400
Listen, I've had a good life.

02:42.500 --> 02:45.800
You can always be proud of your father
and all of his accomplishments.

02:45.900 --> 02:47.800
Accomplishments?
Go to your room.

02:47.900 --> 02:49.500
Peter, there's no way you could die.

02:49.600 --> 02:52.100
You're the most important character
in this family.

02:53.600 --> 02:56.700
I'll take this one.
But I won't pay a cent over $60.

02:56.800 --> 02:59.200
Sir, that casket costs $1,000.

02:59.300 --> 03:00.700
Okay, $70.
What?

03:00.800 --> 03:03.100
$2,000.
That's twice the cost!

03:03.600 --> 03:04.900
$40.
What?

03:05.000 --> 03:06.900
He doesn't know how to haggle.

03:09.100 --> 03:10.600
Peter, what's going on?

03:10.700 --> 03:14.200
I'm selling all my worldly goods,
so you'll have some cash when I'm dead.

03:14.300 --> 03:18.000
Yeah, a lot of memories here.
Look, my first bike.

03:18.100 --> 03:20.300
Boy, I had so much fun playing with that.

03:21.200 --> 03:22.900
More tea, Mr. Bike?

03:23.500 --> 03:26.800
Peter, this is ridiculous.
You're going to be fine.

03:27.100 --> 03:29.800
Dad, the doctor called.
Your test results are in.

03:32.900 --> 03:36.900
This doesn't look very good.
No, this doesn't look very good at all.

03:37.900 --> 03:40.800
My nephew drew my portrait.
It doesn't look a thing like me.

03:40.900 --> 03:42.400
Look at the nose. It's all...

03:42.500 --> 03:44.600
Will you just tell us about Peter's tests?

03:44.700 --> 03:47.700
Okay. Mr. Griffin,
all your tests came back negative.

03:47.800 --> 03:50.900
As it turns out, the lump on your chest
was just a fatty corpuscle.

03:51.000 --> 03:54.300
Fatty corpuscle? Wait a minute.
How the hell can a dead comedian...

03:54.400 --> 03:57.300
...from the silent movie era
be lodged in my left bosom?

03:57.400 --> 03:59.000
Mr. Griffin, I'm saying you're fine.

03:59.100 --> 04:01.400
I'm fine? What?
Are you coming on to me now?

04:01.500 --> 04:05.600
Peter, he's not coming on to you.
He's trying to tell you that you're healthy.

04:06.600 --> 04:07.700
Can't it be both?

04:12.600 --> 04:14.400
My sweetie is okay.

04:14.500 --> 04:17.800
Better than okay, Lois.
From now on, I'm gonna appreciate...

04:17.900 --> 04:21.200
...all the little things in life,
like you and the kids.

04:21.300 --> 04:24.100
Is this the price of my bill
or my phone number?

04:24.200 --> 04:25.800
Your phone number.

04:29.500 --> 04:33.700
It's still pretty pricey!
Peter, who cares how much it is?

04:33.800 --> 04:38.000
You've just got the most important
bill of all, a clean bill of health.

04:38.100 --> 04:41.200
Jeez, Lois. How long you been waiting
to crack out that gem?

04:41.300 --> 04:43.900
This sucks, Brian.
Why should I have to pay this?

04:44.000 --> 04:47.400
- There's nothing wrong with me.
- Too bad you're not dying.

04:47.500 --> 04:50.600
Wait a second. That's it!
They can't make a dead guy pay his bill.

04:50.700 --> 04:54.400
All I gotta do is write "deceased"
right here where it says "name."

04:54.500 --> 04:58.200
And where it says "sex,"
I'll write, "No, thanks. I'm dead."

04:58.300 --> 04:59.900
It's bulletproof.

05:03.200 --> 05:05.500
But you promised
the fat one would perish.

05:05.600 --> 05:09.900
I know. Isn't it wonderful, honey?
Your father is alive and well...

05:10.000 --> 05:12.400
...and we can be a family for a good long...

05:16.300 --> 05:17.700
Who are you?

05:17.800 --> 05:21.500
I'm Calista Flockhart. Who the
hell do you think I am? I'm Death.

05:21.900 --> 05:23.800
Which one of you is Peter Griffin?

05:25.100 --> 05:26.200
He is.

05:29.700 --> 05:32.100
Come on, man.
Which one of you is Peter Griffin?

05:33.200 --> 05:34.900
This is Peter Griffin.

05:36.200 --> 05:37.700
That's a good one.

05:43.300 --> 05:44.300
Why are you...

05:44.400 --> 05:47.200
No, wait.
I'm not finished holding my sides.

05:51.300 --> 05:52.200
Why are...

05:58.000 --> 05:59.000
Why...

06:07.600 --> 06:10.200
Why are you here?
The doctor said Peter was okay.

06:10.300 --> 06:12.400
The doctor!
I guess he must know, right?

06:12.500 --> 06:15.800
I mean, he's a doctor and everything,
and I'm just Death!

06:15.900 --> 06:18.900
Excuse me. Hello!
I'm Stewie. Big fan.

06:19.000 --> 06:21.900
Death, you made a mistake.
I'm not supposed to be dead.

06:22.000 --> 06:23.800
I made a mistake? What's this?

06:25.100 --> 06:26.800
Peter, is that your handwriting?

06:28.200 --> 06:29.700
How did you get that?

06:29.800 --> 06:31.600
Your HMO emailed it to me.

06:31.700 --> 06:35.100
I know my doctor was hitting on me,
but you don't have to call him names.

06:35.300 --> 06:37.900
I don't care what that says!
You can't take my husband!

06:38.000 --> 06:41.000
Mother! Where are your manners?
Don't argue with our guest!

06:41.100 --> 06:44.700
Won't you join us for dinner?
Oh, no. I don't want to impose.

06:45.100 --> 06:47.100
Is that turkey?
Yes, Death.

06:47.200 --> 06:51.800
We were in the middle of a turkey dinner
to celebrate Peter's good health.

06:52.000 --> 06:52.900
Do you mind?

06:53.000 --> 06:56.100
Mind? Of course not.
It would be an honor.

06:56.200 --> 07:00.900
No, it would be a privilege. Oh, dear.
Listen to me prattling on like a schoolgirl.

07:01.300 --> 07:05.000
Come, come.
You, heat up some gravy for our guest!

07:05.500 --> 07:08.400
My last helping of white meat
was drier than Oscar Wilde.

07:14.900 --> 07:16.300
How did you do that?

07:16.400 --> 07:18.900
Let's just say,
when I was younger...

07:19.100 --> 07:23.300
...I did some films
I'm not particularly proud of.

07:23.400 --> 07:24.900
That does it for me.

07:25.000 --> 07:26.800
Wait! You can't go.

07:27.100 --> 07:30.500
After dinner,
we usually go into the living room...

07:30.600 --> 07:33.800
...and live for another 40 or 50 years.

07:33.900 --> 07:35.800
40 or... Let's go.

07:39.000 --> 07:43.000
I guess this is good-bye.
Meg, you're the man of the family now.

07:43.100 --> 07:44.000
Be strong.

07:44.700 --> 07:45.900
Daddy.

07:46.500 --> 07:49.700
Stewie, I guess I'm not gonna be here
to see you become a man.

07:49.800 --> 07:52.700
Yes. I think we all know
what that's going to be like.

07:55.400 --> 07:58.900
A 20-minute call to Larchmont?
Who do we know in Larchmont?

07:59.100 --> 08:00.600
My sister-in-law.

08:00.800 --> 08:04.800
Yes, right. Right. Carol. Yes.
That's right. How is Carol?

08:04.900 --> 08:06.500
- Brian.
- Oh, God.

08:07.900 --> 08:10.600
- Daddy, can I come with you?
- Ask your mother.

08:10.700 --> 08:12.400
No, you can't go with him!

08:12.500 --> 08:14.600
- Oh, Peter.
- Lois.

08:18.800 --> 08:21.800
Okay, that's good. Come on now.

08:26.400 --> 08:30.300
Hey, Death, you got a file on me?
Yeah, it's in the car, I think.

08:30.400 --> 08:33.300
Does it mention that I ran two weeks
of Junior Varsity track?

08:34.300 --> 08:38.400
Let's not do this. I caught Flo Jo.
You don't think I can catch you?

08:40.400 --> 08:41.700
My ankle!

08:43.100 --> 08:46.400
Yeah, listen,
don't help or anything. I'm totally fine.

08:47.400 --> 08:48.500
Damn Irish.

08:51.500 --> 08:54.700
Yeah. That felt good,
dropping me on the couch like that.

08:54.800 --> 08:58.400
Here's some Tylenol.
Great. Tylenol. I asked for Advil.

08:58.500 --> 09:00.300
But, you know, whatever. That's good.

09:00.400 --> 09:03.000
I got a B-plus in Health.
Is there anything I can do?

09:03.100 --> 09:06.700
Why don't you boil some water
and rip up some sheets there, Einstein.

09:06.900 --> 09:08.300
It's a sprained ankle.

09:08.400 --> 09:11.300
I have to stay off it for a while.
Not here.

09:11.400 --> 09:13.400
Why?
You tried to kill me!

09:13.500 --> 09:16.200
Besides, how are we supposed
to explain you to Mr. Roper?

09:16.300 --> 09:19.500
It's okay, Death.
You just worry about feeling better.

09:19.600 --> 09:21.000
What the hell are you doing?

09:21.100 --> 09:25.400
Peter, don't you see?
As long as he's here, you can't die.

09:26.400 --> 09:28.100
Go on.
That's it.

09:28.200 --> 09:31.500
Wait a minute.
So no matter what I do, I won't die?

09:33.200 --> 09:35.500
Make yourself at home, Death.

09:35.600 --> 09:38.100
I'm going out for a while.
Wait.

09:38.200 --> 09:41.200
You can't tell anyone I'm here.
For if humanity discovers...

09:41.300 --> 09:45.400
...l'm no longer lurking in the shadows,
consequences will be dire.

09:46.800 --> 09:48.800
Go on.
That's it.

09:49.400 --> 09:51.000
What the hell do you see in him?

09:51.000 --> 09:51.200
What the hell do you see in him?

09:51.600 --> 09:53.100
Peter, where are you going?

09:53.200 --> 09:55.900
Lois, 10 minutes ago,
I was staring Death in the face.

09:56.000 --> 09:58.000
Now that I've been given another chance...

09:58.100 --> 10:01.200
...l'm gonna do the one thing
I've always dreamed of doing.

10:01.500 --> 10:03.300
I'm gonna jump off this building.

10:03.400 --> 10:07.700
Could you repeat that, please, Peter?
I believe I had something crazy in my ear.

10:07.900 --> 10:08.800
Hold the phone.

10:09.000 --> 10:11.000
You took me away from
a Swedish girlie-girl...

10:11.100 --> 10:13.400
...and her paralyzed,
but trusting, cousin for this?

10:13.500 --> 10:16.100
- $1,000 says I live.
- $1,000, huh?

10:16.200 --> 10:17.400
- What the hell?
- Okay.

10:29.000 --> 10:31.100
Look at that. I beat my loogie.

10:35.900 --> 10:37.300
It's your turn, Death.

10:37.400 --> 10:40.900
I know I should find this ironic,
but I'm just bored as hell.

10:41.000 --> 10:42.200
How old is this TV?

10:42.300 --> 10:44.800
You can probably get
the DuMont Network on this thing.

10:44.900 --> 10:47.900
Peter is a good man
and a wonderful father.

10:48.000 --> 10:49.100
Here it comes.

10:49.200 --> 10:52.600
Could you please find it in your heart
to spare him?

10:52.700 --> 10:55.400
After all, it isn't really his time.

10:55.500 --> 10:57.700
What did you use
for this cocoa, crap?

10:57.800 --> 11:01.000
If you want me to make it again...
Sorry, my fault.

11:01.100 --> 11:03.900
I just assumed you were gonna make it
with milk, not crap!

11:04.000 --> 11:05.700
I'll be right back.

11:05.900 --> 11:08.500
I brought you a magazine.
Glamour, great.

11:08.600 --> 11:11.700
I can learn how to please my man.
Go get me an Entertainment Weekly.

11:11.800 --> 11:14.900
I hear it's got a great picture of me
sneaking up on Tom Snyder.

11:36.000 --> 11:37.400
Victory is mine!

11:41.000 --> 11:43.800
Wow. I should really
watch where I'm going.

11:44.600 --> 11:45.600
What the deuce?

11:47.100 --> 11:48.100
Of course!

11:48.700 --> 11:52.800
It seems with Death incapacitated,
my matricidal efforts are futile.

11:53.300 --> 11:55.800
I must do all I can to accelerate
his convalescence.

11:58.400 --> 12:00.500
"Knick-knack paddywhack,
give a dog a bone"

12:06.600 --> 12:10.800
I can't believe you drank 300 bottles
of beer without succumbing...

12:10.900 --> 12:12.400
...to alcohol poisoning.

12:12.800 --> 12:14.800
Peter, are you a witch?

12:15.200 --> 12:19.400
Yeah. But don't tell anyone.
The consequences could be dire!

12:21.700 --> 12:26.000
You guys, I bet I can go up to each one
of those scary-looking bikers and say:

12:26.200 --> 12:28.500
"Aren't you Richard Simmons?"

12:28.700 --> 12:31.400
- Peter, no!
- Now you're being brainless.

12:32.000 --> 12:34.300
Aren't you Richard Simmons?

12:36.000 --> 12:40.900
Aren't you Richard Simmons' best friend,
Richard Simmons?

12:41.000 --> 12:42.000
Shut up!

13:13.100 --> 13:14.300
That feels good.

13:14.400 --> 13:18.400
Actually, kid, I kind of fell into this gig.
I really wanted to be a wood nymph.

13:18.500 --> 13:21.500
Man, the second Dad found out,
he started in with the whole:

13:21.600 --> 13:26.300
"I have no son. I have no son,"
and Mom just stood there.

13:26.800 --> 13:29.700
Yes. Mothers can be quite
the botheration, can't they?

13:29.800 --> 13:31.900
That's why we've got to get you well.

13:32.000 --> 13:33.400
- What was that?
- Nothing!

13:33.500 --> 13:35.300
Stewie, leave Death alone.

13:35.400 --> 13:38.300
He's okay.
He reminds me a lot of me at that age.

13:38.400 --> 13:42.100
I hope his teen years go better than mine.
Boy, talk about awkward.

13:43.700 --> 13:47.400
Oh, Sandy! Sandy!

13:50.400 --> 13:53.500
Sandy? Not again.

13:53.700 --> 13:55.700
I'm gonna be a virgin forever.

13:56.900 --> 13:58.300
Or am I?

14:02.100 --> 14:03.700
Can we please talk about Peter?

14:03.800 --> 14:07.900
He has so much to live for, Death.
He loves his children and me...

14:08.100 --> 14:10.700
Okay. I'll spare his life.

14:11.200 --> 14:13.800
But you owe me, if you get my drift.

14:16.900 --> 14:20.200
What the hell are you doing?
I was talking about another fruit cup.

14:20.300 --> 14:21.500
Not bad, though.

14:21.600 --> 14:24.300
Peter,
Death just agreed to let you live.

14:24.400 --> 14:28.000
Oh, man. This really is my night.
I get to live, and I'm on TV.

14:28.100 --> 14:31.000
Our top story tonight,
the rules of death no longer apply.

14:31.100 --> 14:32.300
That's right, Tom.

14:32.400 --> 14:37.300
Our own Asian reporter, Trisha Takanawa,
filed this report, all by herself!

14:37.600 --> 14:41.000
I'm here with Peter Griffin,
the man who claims he withstood...

14:41.200 --> 14:43.900
...a barrage of bullets and did not die.

14:44.400 --> 14:47.300
Peter, are you saying
that if I shoot you in the head...

14:47.400 --> 14:51.400
...with this Channel 5 pistol,
you'll be completely unharmed?

14:51.500 --> 14:53.500
Why don't you give it a shot?

14:55.500 --> 14:57.400
Okay, here goes.

15:00.800 --> 15:01.800
What have I done?

15:04.800 --> 15:06.300
You're awful.

15:07.200 --> 15:10.200
- Fascinating story, Tom.
- It sure is, Diane.

15:10.300 --> 15:13.300
And since the laws of death
no longer apply, I can do this.

15:16.000 --> 15:17.300
That's right, Tom.

15:20.200 --> 15:21.900
And now it's time for sports.

15:22.900 --> 15:26.600
The whole world is laughing
at me. This is high school all over again.

15:26.700 --> 15:30.300
Well, I'll show them! I'll show all of them!
Oh, my God, that hurts!

15:30.400 --> 15:34.200
You're not killing anyone tonight, mister!
Not on that ankle.

15:34.300 --> 15:37.300
This is all your fault.
And there's only one solution.

15:38.000 --> 15:40.200
You have to go out there and do my job.

15:40.300 --> 15:43.000
You have to be Death!

15:50.900 --> 15:53.700
Boy, this doesn't leave much
to the imagination.

15:53.800 --> 15:56.400
Death, there is no way
Peter can do your job.

15:56.500 --> 15:58.100
He could never kill anyone.

15:58.200 --> 16:01.100
Yeah! I've thought about it,
like in church and stuff...

16:01.200 --> 16:03.700
...but I don't think I could ever do
what you do.

16:03.800 --> 16:05.100
So you're better than me?

16:05.200 --> 16:08.400
I'm tired of always being the bad guy.
What I do has to be done.

16:08.500 --> 16:11.300
He's right. You've disturbed
the natural order.

16:11.400 --> 16:12.800
People need to be able to die.

16:18.100 --> 16:19.100
No!

16:20.200 --> 16:23.200
- Actually, I think I'm gonna be okay.
- Oh, Jack.

16:23.300 --> 16:26.000
Now we can get married
and everything you promised.

16:26.200 --> 16:27.400
Yeah, about that...

16:28.000 --> 16:30.700
...I was pretty sure I was gonna die...

16:30.800 --> 16:34.600
...because there's this girl in New York,
and it's getting kind of serious.

16:34.700 --> 16:37.200
But thanks for letting me draw you naked.

16:37.500 --> 16:39.900
I still can't believe you let me do that!

16:40.100 --> 16:44.300
You're saying the only way to make
the world right is for me to kill someone?

16:44.400 --> 16:47.700
You could kill Lois.
No. One death isn't gonna do it.

16:47.800 --> 16:51.400
You have to do something that will
get everyone's attention, something huge.

16:51.500 --> 16:53.300
How about if you blow up the earth?

16:53.400 --> 16:55.700
Too huge.
But you're thinking. I like that.

16:55.800 --> 16:58.200
You could kill any girls
who are prettier than me.

16:58.400 --> 17:01.200
That would just leave England.
Wait. I have it.

17:02.200 --> 17:06.200
I'm a genius.
You'll kill the kids from Dawson's Creek!

17:06.300 --> 17:09.000
I knew it! As soon as that show
came on the air, I said:

17:09.100 --> 17:11.400
"I'm gonna be the one
who has to kill these kids."

17:11.500 --> 17:14.500
It's true. He did say it.
Hot, young celebrities.

17:14.600 --> 17:16.100
It's perfect!

17:16.300 --> 17:19.400
The kids are on their way to LA
to renegotiate their contracts.

17:19.500 --> 17:24.300
But their plane is gonna be making
a little stopover in Rhode Island.

17:24.500 --> 17:27.000
If you go now, you'll catch them.
No way.

17:27.200 --> 17:30.600
I'm not doing your dirty work.
There's no way I'm getting on that plane.

17:30.700 --> 17:33.600
Absolutely no way, and that's final.

17:34.800 --> 17:36.300
See? I'm still here.

17:36.400 --> 17:38.800
There's nothing you can say
that'll change my mind.

17:38.900 --> 17:40.800
You kill them, or I kill you.

17:41.600 --> 17:42.700
Crap!

17:45.300 --> 17:46.300
Nice plant.

17:47.500 --> 17:50.300
Note to self, do not go to the bathroom.

17:50.500 --> 17:52.900
James,
your last movie killed at the box office.

17:53.000 --> 17:54.500
Your Q-rating's through the roof.

17:54.600 --> 17:57.300
It's time we ditched the WB
and concentrate on features.

17:57.400 --> 18:00.200
I don't know who you are,
but just because you're sitting...

18:00.300 --> 18:03.300
...across from me doesn't mean
you can give me career advice.

18:03.700 --> 18:06.000
- Will you sign my ass?
- You have a pen?

18:07.900 --> 18:11.100
Hello, Death?
Guess where I'm calling from?

18:11.700 --> 18:13.300
A plane!
That's great.

18:13.400 --> 18:15.400
Are those kids on board?
Yeah.

18:15.500 --> 18:18.500
About that,
I don't think I can go through with it.

18:18.600 --> 18:22.300
Peter, listen, without death,
the world would be a terrible place.

18:22.400 --> 18:24.900
Imagine a world
where Hitler was still alive.

18:25.700 --> 18:29.600
Today on Hitler,
we'll be talking with Christian Slater.

18:30.000 --> 18:33.200
Now, they tell me in your next movie,
we get to see your butt.

18:35.100 --> 18:38.000
Yes, you do.
Can we see it right now?

18:40.300 --> 18:42.400
All right.
He's going to do it!

18:42.500 --> 18:46.300
If you're going to be in L.A.
And would like tickets to Hitler...

18:46.400 --> 18:48.900
...call 213-du werdest
eine Krankenschwester brauchen!

18:49.000 --> 18:53.000
Peter, all you gotta do is sit there.
The plane is gonna crash in LA.

18:53.300 --> 18:56.200
Pilot error. Big mess. Everybody dies.

18:56.800 --> 18:59.100
Jeez, everybody?
Except you.

18:59.700 --> 19:01.900
Hold on, I'm getting another call. Brenda?

19:02.400 --> 19:04.300
It's still me.
Brenda?

19:04.600 --> 19:07.500
Yes? Just kidding, it's still me.

19:09.000 --> 19:12.600
We now begin our final approach
into Los Angeles International.

19:12.700 --> 19:15.700
If you look out the window,
you'll see the San Fernando Valley...

19:15.800 --> 19:18.900
...where my brother Gary makes
a very nice living directing porn.

19:19.000 --> 19:20.900
We'll be on the ground in 10 minutes.

19:24.900 --> 19:28.200
"We like being alive,
we like being alive

19:28.300 --> 19:31.600
"We like being, oh, we like being,
oh, we like being alive"

19:31.700 --> 19:33.300
I guess it's their time.

19:39.900 --> 19:42.700
Boy, for a teacher,
you sure make love good.

19:42.800 --> 19:46.300
Actually, it's "well," Pacey.
You mean to say, I make love "well."

19:46.900 --> 19:49.000
- You're good to go again, right?
- Yeah.

19:49.100 --> 19:52.500
Peter? Hello? Peter,
are you there? I can hear you breathing?

19:52.600 --> 19:56.300
Yeah, I'm here. And you can forget it.
I've changed my mind.

19:56.400 --> 19:59.400
I don't care if you do kill me,
I'm not gonna kill those kids.

19:59.500 --> 20:02.200
If they die, I'll have nothing
to watch on Wednesdays...

20:04.400 --> 20:06.600
...other than the fine programs on Fox.

20:10.900 --> 20:12.000
Open up in there!

20:12.200 --> 20:16.000
What are you doing? You're not a pilot.
I know every pilot in the world!

20:16.100 --> 20:19.200
I'm here to keep you from making an error.
A pilot error.

20:20.000 --> 20:22.100
Jeez, I probably should've worn mittens!

20:23.900 --> 20:25.300
Nice going, fat...

20:25.400 --> 20:29.000
I was just trying to save your lives.
But now you're all gonna die.

20:29.100 --> 20:31.500
- No one can land this plane.
- I can.

20:32.000 --> 20:34.100
Thank God! It's Karen Black!

20:35.600 --> 20:38.200
She landed a busted plane in Airport '75?

20:39.500 --> 20:41.100
It was a movie in the '70s.

20:42.900 --> 20:44.900
You damn kids with your music.

20:45.700 --> 20:47.400
Both of the pilots were killed.

20:47.500 --> 20:50.400
Fortunately for the other passengers,
actress Karen Black...

20:50.500 --> 20:54.200
...star of such films as Nashville
and Five Easy Pieces, was on board.

20:54.300 --> 20:58.300
Hats off to Miss Black for proving
once again that, given the opportunity...

20:58.400 --> 21:01.500
...actresses over 50 can land large aircraft.

21:02.000 --> 21:04.100
Karen Black. What an obscure reference!

21:04.200 --> 21:07.600
What the hell? I told you to waste
the Dawson's Creek kids.

21:07.700 --> 21:09.800
You're missing
the important thing here.

21:09.900 --> 21:12.900
You said you wanted everyone to know
the rules of death apply.

21:13.000 --> 21:15.500
Now the whole world does.
I guess so.

21:15.600 --> 21:19.300
My ankle's starting to feel better.
I should probably get out of your hair.

21:19.400 --> 21:20.900
But you just got here!

21:21.100 --> 21:23.800
We can stay in touch, can't we?
What's your e-mail?

21:23.900 --> 21:27.100
Mine is "loismustdie," all one word,
"@yahoo.com."

21:27.200 --> 21:28.900
Wait a second. Death?

21:29.000 --> 21:32.000
I used to fear you,
but now I'm glad we met.

21:32.600 --> 21:36.100
Because you've given me a great gift.
The complete Boz Scaggs.

21:36.200 --> 21:38.500
How did you know?
I just had a feeling.

21:39.100 --> 21:41.600
We're gonna miss you, Death.
Don't worry.

21:41.700 --> 21:43.900
I'll be back really, really soon.

21:46.000 --> 21:47.000
Is he joking?

21:48.900 --> 21:50.400
Okay, see you later.

21:50.401 --> 22:51.401
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru